WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.800
Who are the Top 10 Greatest Warriors in A
Song of Ice and Fire?

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.950
Which characters are best at fighting, in
their prime years, with their usual weapons

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.070
and armour?

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.460
This ranking is based on the books, in the
time period of the main series and Robert’s

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.460
Rebellion.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.320
No dragons or warging or magic allowed, giants
and white walkers don’t count.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.960
The number ten best warrior is Victarion Greyjoy,
“The Iron Captain”.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.869
Victarion wasn’t in the TV show.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:31.569
But he’s an uncle of Theon and Asha.

00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:35.780
And Victarion is renowned among the ironborn
as a fearsome warrior.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:41.690
He’s a big man, strong as a bull and about
as smart as a bull, but that just makes him

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:42.690
braver.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.969
Victarion wears heavy plate armour even in
sea battles – which is dangerous, cause

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:51.469
he could drown if he falls overboard, but
Victarion is fearless.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:57.059
He lives to fight, he was put on this earth
to deal death with his axe.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:01.750
In Book 4, Victarion singlehandedly slaughters
a bunch of men in battle.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:07.490
Then he kills a knight called Talbert Serry
– Serry is fast, but Victarion’s fast

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.750
too, catching Serry’s sword in his armoured
hand.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.750
Victarion’s hand gets wounded and infected.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:21.360
So a red priest called Moqorro heals Victarion’s
hand with magic, and now Vic’s arm is burned

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.579
black, and smoking, and is stronger than ever.

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:30.810
Victarion lifts a man in the air and kills
him with just this bare hand.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:37.259
So with his new super-strong barbeque fist,
Victarion may be even more dangerous than

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:38.579
before.

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:43.009
But we never see Victarion fight any really
skilled opponents.

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:46.579
Talbert Serry is not a particularly renowned
knight.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:50.090
And Victarion’s bravery does border on stupidity.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:55.420
So while Victarion is powerful, there are
better fighters.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.840
Number nine is Loras Tyrell, “the Knight
of Flowers”.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.899
Loras is just sixteen years old in Book 1,
but he’s already famous as a great knight.

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:09.320
He’s graceful, and quick, and very skilled
at fighting.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.510
Author George Martin said Loras is one of
the best swordsmen in Westeros.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.560
And he’s extremely good at jousting in tournaments.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.800
But Oberyn Martell questions whether Loras
is any good in actual battle.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.590
So what fights has Loras won?

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:28.300
We see Loras lose a fight with Brienne in
a melee.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:33.590
Loras kills two knights – who were on his
side, out of mad grief.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.670
Loras apparently fought “magnificently”
at the Battle of the Blackwater, though not

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.010
as magnificently as his brother Garlan.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:46.530
In Book 5, Loras leads a savage assault on
Dragonstone, and kills a bunch of men, but

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:52.260
Loras gets badly wounded and doused in boiling
oil, and is expected to die.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:58.000
So Loras is a talented fighter, but he doesn’t
have many great feats of battle.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.830
And his arrogant recklessness is a weakness
that may’ve just got him killed.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:06.190
Jaime thinks Loras has the potential to be
great.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:10.080
But so far that potential is unfulfilled.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.940
Number eight is Brienne, the Maid of Tarth.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.220
Brienne is freakishly big and strong.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.129
She’s well over six feet tall, bigger and
stronger than Jaime.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:25.580
She’s a skilled fighter, she moves shockingly
fast in battle.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:30.340
And she’s even more dangerous with the Valyrian
steel sword Oathkeeper.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:35.459
In Book 2, Brienne wins a melee at Renly’s
camp – she’s the last standing of one

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:41.500
hundred and sixteen knights, and she personally
defeats Loras Tyrell, one of the best knights

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.500
alive.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.240
Though Loras claims that she won with a trick,
by tackling him.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.310
Brienne often uses her size and strength to
overwhelm opponents – her fighting style

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.620
is similar to that of her ancestor, Duncan
the Tall.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:00.310
After Renly dies, Brienne fights off a bunch
of Renly’s men, with speed and skill.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:05.030
In Book 3, Brienne fights Jaime Lannister,
one of the best swordsmen in Westeros.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:11.599
It’s a long, hard fight, but try as he might,
Jaime can’t kill her, and ultimately, Brienne

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:13.680
beats Jaime.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.270
Though she realises that Jaime is weakened
from months of imprisonment, and his hands

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.850
are chained together, so Brienne thinks that
Jaime would have won if he was at his full

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:23.870
strength.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.680
In Book 4, Brienne fights some of the Brave
Companions, or Bloody Mummers, a mercenary

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.820
group of absolute frothing psychos.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.750
Brienne kills three of them in a one v three
fight with a little help from Pod.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:44.430
And in the next fight she kills Rorge, the
Mad Dog of Saltpans, but then Biter eats some

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.390
of Brienne’s face, before she’s saved
by Gendry.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.960
So Brienne is often underestimated for being
a woman.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:58.040
But with her great strength, skill, and sheer
tenacity, Brienne wins a lot of fights, and

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.830
defeats some of the greatest knights in Westeros.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.530
Number seven is Garlan Tyrell “the Gallant”.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.450
Garlan wasn’t in the TV show.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.330
But in the books, he’s an older brother
of Loras.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.500
Garlan isn’t as famous as Loras.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.960
But he is bigger and stronger.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.650
And Loras says that Garlan is a better swordsman
than him.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.860
Author George Martin said the same thing.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:26.720
We see that Garlan often trains by fighting
three or four men at once, so that he’s

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.310
better prepared for real battle.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:33.930
Garlan fights “magnificently” at the Battle
of the Blackwater – he kills Guyard Morrigen

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.960
in single combat “and a dozen other great
knights”.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:42.990
When Margaery faces a trial by combat, it’s
Garlan she wants as her champion.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.210
So we haven’t seen much of Garlan.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.930
But he’s clearly an exceptional warrior.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:53.090
Number six is Gregor Clegane, “the Mountain
That Rides”.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:56.200
Gregor is monstrously “huge”.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:01.980
Almost eight feet tall and weighing four hundred
pounds, or two hundred kilos, “all of it

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:02.980
muscle”.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:08.130
Gregor is inhumanly strong, he often cuts
men in half with a single blow.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:14.460
Gregor wields a two-handed greatsword in one
hand, so he’s got a monstrously long reach.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.120
He’s surprisingly quick, and he doesn’t
seem to feel pain.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:23.390
“No other knight in the realm inspires such
terror” as the Mountain.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.030
The Hound says “No one could ever withstand
Gregor”.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.570
But what are his accomplishments in combat?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:35.920
In Book 1, the Mountain attacks Loras and
the Hound, and tries to kill them, but he

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:36.920
fails.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:41.090
The Hound stops the Mountain, deflects his
massive blows.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:46.020
The Mountain fights in some battles in the
war – he kills Beric Dondarrion – twice.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.030
He kills Raymun Darry and his horse with a
single blow.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:54.730
Then in Tyrion’s trial by combat, Gregor
fights Oberyn Martell.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:07:00.990
And Oberyn uses his speed and skill and poison
to mortally wound Gregor, impaling him with

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:05.210
a spear – though Gregor still kills Oberyn
in the end.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:10.660
Then the mad scientist Qyburn transforms the
Mountain into a mysterious undead warrior

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.730
called Robert Strong.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:18.260
This silent knight may be even more dangerous
than the Mountain was, but we haven’t seen

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.760
yet him in action in the books.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:26.170
So the Mountain is extremely dangerous, but
we’ve never seen him beat a really top-tier

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.450
opponent.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:31.290
Skilled warriors like Oberyn and the Hound
can stop him.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:35.510
So number five is the Hound, Sandor Clegane.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.130
The Hound is a big man, tall, “muscled like
a bull”.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:43.250
And he’s “quick”, fighting with a terrible
“savagery”.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.720
Sandor is a twisted, bitter man whose greatest
joy in life is killing.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:55.410
He’s been killing men since he was twelve
years old – knights, lords, women and children.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:08:01.170
Everyone knows the Hound is “deadly with
a sword”, and his snarling dog helm is widely

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.170
feared.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:06.410
Even Jaime says the Hound is a “dangerous”,
“powerful” warrior.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:10.550
Author George Martin said the Hound is one
of the greatest swordsmen in Westeros.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.490
And we’ve seen this in action.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:15.540
In Book 1, the Hound stops the Mountain.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:20.210
Despite all the Mountain’s strength and
rage he can’t kill his brother.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:24.090
The Hound flees the Battle of the Blackwater,
because he’s afraid of fire.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:28.540
But in Book 3, he overcomes his fear to kill
Beric Dondarrion.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.640
Killing Beric is basically a Clegane family
tradition.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:36.480
The Hound kills some men at the Twins in a
three v one fight.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:40.820
Then with the help of Arya, he kills some
of Gregor’s men, even though he’s blind

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:41.830
drunk.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.480
The Hound’s wounds get infected, and he’s
left for dead.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:50.590
But in Book 4, the Hound seems to have survived
and found a peaceful life as a monk.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.140
Maybe he’ll return to fight his zombie brother
in the next book.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:09:00.500
So the Hound has a proven record as a skilled,
powerful warrior.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.620
But the fourth best warrior in Westeros is
a young Robert Baratheon.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:09.900
In Book 1, Robert is fat, drunk, and past
his prime.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.330
But twenty years ago, when he took the Throne,
Robert was “the fiercest warrior of the

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.330
realm”.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:20.250
He was six and a half feet tall, towering
over his enemies in his armour and antlered

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.250
helmet.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:25.960
He had “a giant’s strength”, wielding
a huge iron warhammer that Ned Stark could

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.420
barely lift.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.690
In his rebellion against the Targaryens, Robert
won many battles, fighting fearlessly on the

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:33.810
front lines.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:39.480
At Gulltown, he was the first up the walls
and killed Lord Grafton by his own hand.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:46.490
At Summerhall, Robert won three battles in
one day, and killed Lord Fell in single combat.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:51.800
He lost a battle at Ashford, but he won the
Battle of the Bells and killed six men including

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.280
the famous knight Myles Mooton.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:10:00.150
Finally, Robert won the Battle of the Trident,
personally killing Prince Rhaegar Targaryen,

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:02.980
who was renowned as a skilled warrior.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:06.030
And so Robert won the war and became King
of Westeros.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:09.870
Robert is one of the most successful warriors
ever.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:15.790
He won all these battles, personally killing
many knights and lords, and no one ever managed

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.450
to kill him.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:22.490
Except, eventually, for a pig, and his wife,
and his crippling alcoholism.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:28.850
But in his prime, Robert was one of the greatest
warriors in Westeros.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:34.150
Number three is Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer,
before he lost his hand.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:38.760
Barristan Selmy thinks of Jaime as one of
the best natural swordsmen he’s seen.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:43.500
Jaime says that in his prime he was bigger,
stronger and quicker than Loras.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:49.190
He’s confident that with his skill and speed,
he could beat the Mountain and the Hound.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:54.660
Author George Martin often names Jaime as
one of, if not the, best fighters in Westeros.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.440
He said Jaime would beat Aragorn in a fight.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.330
He said Jaime would beat Hermione in a fight.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:03.750
He said Jaime would beat a cult of Cthulhu.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:08.210
Jaime won a tournament melee when he was just
thirteen years old.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:13.140
At fifteen, he fought the Kingswood Brotherhood,
and held his own against the notorious Smiling

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.140
Knight.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:18.880
Jaime was knighted by Arthur Dayne, and became
the youngest Kingsguard ever.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:24.340
In the main series, he kicks ass in several
battles, covering himself in glory.

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:28.360
He cuts through Edmure’s army “like an
axe through ripe cheese”.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:32.670
At the Whispering Wood, he fights through
the northern army and almost kills Robb Stark

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:38.050
– he only stops because his sword gets stuck
in a northman’s neck.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:42.830
Even after being imprisoned and weakened for
months, he still almost beats Brienne.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:47.870
Brienne thinks at his full strength, “No
knight in the Seven Kingdoms could have stood

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.640
against him”.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.200
Once Jaime loses his hand, he’s no longer
a great fighter.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:59.190
But his battles, his reputation, and the words
of the author, show that Jaime is the greatest

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.680
warrior of his generation.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:04.770
Number two is a young Barristan Selmy.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:11.060
Barristan the Bold is widely recognised as
the greatest knight alive, a living legend.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.820
When he was young, Barristan “was the finest
sword in the Seven Kingdoms”.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:18.430
And he has a long list of accomplishments
in combat.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:22.200
Barristan rode in his first tournament at
ten years old.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.520
At sixteen, he performed “great feats of
prowess” in a tournament, and defeated Duncan

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.470
the Tall, Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:34.770
At 23, he joined the Kingsguard himself, and
won many more victories in tournaments and

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:35.770
melees.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:36.770
He “Defeated Lormelle Long Lance and Cedrik
Storm” and Blackshield, he defeated all

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.560
challengers at the Silver Bridge.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.360
Barristan defeated Simon Toyne of the Kingswood
Brotherhood.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:48.400
Barristan ended the War of the Ninepenny Kings,
by killing Maelys the Monstrous in “single

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.400
combat”.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:53.279
And Barristan ended the Defiance of Duskendale.

00:12:53.279 --> 00:12:57.600
King Aerys Targaryen got kidnapped and held
hostage by House Darklyn.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:02.720
So in an act of crazy courage, Barristan singlehandedly
rescued the king.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:08.130
He climbed the walls of Duskendale with his
bare hands, killed a bunch of guards and knights,

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:12.060
and escaped with Aerys, despite taking an
arrow to his chest.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.340
In the Battle of the Trident, Barristan fought
for the Targaryens, but he was so badass that

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:20.070
when Robert took over, he decided to keep
Barristan on the Kingsguard.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:25.600
In the time of the main series, Barristan
is in his sixties, and he’s still an exceptional

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:26.600
fighter.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.900
Still winning tournaments.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.300
Still better than all the other Kingsguard.

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:34.520
He joins Daenerys and he kills the Titan’s
Bastard with a stick.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:37.120
He kills a deadly Dothraki warrior.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.460
And he leads a cavalry charge in the siege
of Meereen.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:45.750
Barristan has been winning fights for six
decades, and is universally recognised as

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.600
the greatest knight alive.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:52.200
But there is one warrior who is better.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.730
First – some honourable mentions.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:58.800
Oberyn Martell, the Red Viper, has a great
reputation as a warrior, and he’s very skilled,

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.940
but the one time we see him fight, he dies.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:05.710
Bronn is a deadly warrior, Tyrion compares
him to Jaime.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:11.960
Thoros of Myr beats the Hound in melees three
times, probably because Thoros uses flaming

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:12.960
swords.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:19.130
Khal Drogo never loses a fight but we never
see him beat an armoured knight.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:23.839
Greatjon Umber is so tough that when his fingers
get eaten he laughs.

00:14:23.839 --> 00:14:28.700
Mance Rayder became king of the wildlings
by killing a bunch of his rivals.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:33.490
Andrik the Unsmiling is said to be greatest
fighter in the Iron Islands, but we don’t

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.830
know anything about him.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:40.570
Darkstar is said to be “the most dangerous
man in Dorne” – he’s also edgiest emo

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:41.770
in Dorne.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:47.060
And Strong Belwas is such a confident gladiator
that he lets his opponents cut him before

00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:48.590
he kills them.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:55.440
He survives poison, eats liver and onions,
and takes a literal shit on his opponents.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:15:02.140
The kitten Ser Pounce has the impressive combat
feat of scaring off Balerion, a notably fearsome

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.140
tomcat.

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:08.640
However, Ser Pounce fails to prevent Lady
Whiskers from stealing his mouse, so Ser Pounce’s

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:11.170
combat record is mixed at best.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:18.600
But the number one best warrior in Westeros
is Arthur Dayne, the Sword of the Morning.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.010
Arthur died twenty years ago.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:27.130
But he’s remembered as the “deadliest”
of Aerys’ Kingsguard – deadlier than Barristan,

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.480
deadlier than Jaime.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:34.150
Jaime says Arthur could’ve killed five Kingsguard
with his left hand while taking a piss with

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.370
his right.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:39.610
Ned Stark said Arthur was “The finest knight”
he ever saw.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:46.100
Arthur wielded the legendary sword Dawn, said
to be forged from the heart of a meteor.

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:50.940
George Martin said that with Dawn, Arthur
would beat Barristan in a fight.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:55.980
Arthur killed the Smiling Knight, who was
like the Mountain of his time.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:16:01.320
Arthur apparently died fighting Ned Stark,
with the help of Howland Reed.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:05.090
In the show, it’s revealed that Howland
stabbed Arthur in the back – but in the

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:08.160
books, this whole situation is still a mystery.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.840
There’s so much we don’t know about Arthur.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.950
His only fights mentioned in the books are
Ned Stark and the Smiling Knight.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:19.360
We only know he’s the best warrior ever
because the characters and the author say

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.360
so.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:26.480
Many characters think of Arthur with nostalgia,
and rose-tinted glasses.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:32.750
So was he really that great, or is he just
the idealised symbol of a noble knight?

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:37.170
How can we ever know if he would’ve beaten
the Hound or Brienne in a fight?

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:42.510
George Martin has said the whole idea of ranking
the best fighters is kinda dumb.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.980
There is no objective answer.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:50.120
Who would win in a fight depends on the situation,
on the day, on random chance.

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:54.640
It depends on the relationships and emotions
of the people involved.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:59.850
A Song of Ice and Fire isn’t about the sword-fights
– it’s about the story, the characters

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:01.480
and themes.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:03.270
But we won’t let that stop us.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:08.089
Comment below your top ten best fighters,
or top twenty – how would you rank Oberyn

00:17:08.089 --> 00:17:10.340
and the Greatjon and Belwas?

